From 5fd16d5bc50af54c1628926f9e5812eab8fc6a8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Date: Thu, 7 Mar 2024 17:33:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 580/954] refactor(st-ddr): reduce DDR driver footprint for
 STM32MP2

Remove useless code and files.
Reduce global variables notably by using them as entry parameters for
sub-functions.
Replace some very rarely used enum types by definitions.
Consider only single pstate case in PHY driver.
Fix MISRA and coding rules warnings.
Simplify some algorithms.
Remove all references to undelivered documents.
Reorder CSR definitions.
Fix indentations inside phyinit structure description.
Code and comments minor fixes.
Reaffect procodtctl_program() to LPDDR4, even if no impact.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git ff750ca9ed771cd60f5d3a76fe109ebd4273a939 refactor(st-ddr): reduce DDR driver footprint for STM32MP2]
